      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Based on [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through **credential injection at spawn time**:\n\n1. **Local secrets loading**: A secrets loader reads the Anthropic API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup.\n\n2. **No environment mutation of the Hub**: The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never modified to hold the key.\n\n3. **Child-process injection only**: The key is injected directly into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process immediately before that process starts \u2014 and separately for the Query agent process as well.\n\n4. **Security benefit**: Because the key exists only in the short-lived child processes that actually call the Anthropic API, a compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the credential simply by reading its own environment variables.\n\nThis design keeps credential lifetime minimal and limits exposure: the key is never present in the parent process\u0027s memory or environment, and each child process receives it only when needed.",
      "input_tokens": 4492,
      "output_tokens": 220
    }
